  "answer_text": "While there is **no official, 100% free, 24/7 live video stream** of the MSNBC television channel without a pay-TV subscription or cable login, there are several **legal and official ways** to watch or listen to MSNBC online for free (both permanently and temporarily).\n\n---\n\n### 1. Watch MSNBC Live via Free Trials (Temporary Video)\nIf you need to watch the live television broadcast right now, you can sign up for a free trial with a live TV streaming service. As long as you cancel before the trial period ends, you will not be charged. \n\nThe top services that offer MSNBC and a free trial include:\n*   **Fubo:** Typically offers a **7-day free trial**.\n*   **DirecTV Stream:** Frequently offers a **5-day free trial**.\n*   **YouTube TV:** Often offers a **7-day to 14-day free trial**.\n\n*Note: Be sure to cancel the subscription in your account settings before the trial period ends to avoid being billed.*\n\n---\n\n### 2. Stream MSNBC Live Audio (100% Free, Permanent)\nIf you don't mind only listening, you can stream the **complete, 24/7 live audio broadcast** of MSNBC for free from anywhere in the world. This includes all major shows like *Morning Joe*, *The Rachel Maddow Show*, *The Beat with Ari Melber*, and *The ReidOut*.\n*   **TuneIn:** You can search \"MSNBC\" on TuneIn.com or the TuneIn app to listen to the live audio simulcast for free.\n*   **MS NOW App:** NBC's official app (available on iOS and Android) allows you to stream live audio of MSNBC 24/7 for free. \n\n---\n\n### 3. Watch Show Segments on YouTube (100% Free, On-Demand)\nIf you have a favorite show (like *The Beat* or *The Rachel Maddow Show*) but don't need to watch it precisely live, the **official MSNBC YouTube channel** is your best free option. \n*   MSNBC uploads nearly all of their major daily segments and political commentary in high-definition just a few hours after they air on TV. \n*   This is entirely free, requires no login, and can be watched on any smart TV, phone, or computer.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Use the NBC / MSNBC App \"Preview\"\nIf you download the **MS NOW App** or visit **NBC.com**, you can watch the live video feed of MSNBC for a free **10-minute trial/preview** per day without logging in. \n\n*(If you or a family member already pay for a traditional cable provider, satellite, or a live TV subscription, you can log in to the MS NOW app using those TV credentials to stream the live channel 24/7 for free).*\n\n---\n\n### 5. Alternative: NBC News NOW (100% Free 24/7 Live Video)\nIf you just want live, high-quality news without paying a dime, check out **NBC News NOW**. \n*   This is NBC\u2019s dedicated, 24/7 free streaming news channel. \n*   While it has a different lineup than the MSNBC cable channel, it features live breaking news, reports from NBC correspondents, and live anchors. \n*   You can watch it completely free on platforms like **Pluto TV, Tubi, Samsung TV Plus, The Roku Channel, and YouTube**.",
